t only the impact of the Mediterranean diet on cardiovascular events but also its effects on adiposity and cognitive function. The findings from the study suggest that adherence to the Mediterranean diet is associated with a reduction in cardiovascular events, which may also influence the development of dementia. Overall, the ESTUDIO PREDIMED provides significant insights into the health benefits of the Mediterranean diet, particularly in relation to cardiovascular complications and cognitive health.", "HOMBRES Y MUJERES DE EDAD AVANZADA:Older men and women aged 55 to 80 years with type 2 diabetes and/or multiple cardiovascular risk factors participated in the study.", "COMPLICACIONES CARDIOVASCULARES:Cardiovascular complications refer to serious health issues related to the heart and blood vessels, which the Mediterranean diet aims to prevent.", "EXCESO DE PESO:Exceso de peso, or overweight, is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease, often linked to dietary habits.", "TABAQUISMO:", "CANCER OF THE COLON:Colon cancer is a type of cancer that affects the large intestine, and higher adherence to the Mediterranean diet has been associated with a lower incidence of this disease.", "CANCER OF THE LUNG:Lung cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the lungs, and studies suggest that adherence to the Mediterranean diet may lower its incidence.", "PREDIMED DIABETES:PREDIMED Diabetes is a study that demonstrated the benefits of adherence to a Mediterranean diet in reducing the risk of type 2 diabetes in older adults with high cardiometabolic risk.", "SOCIETADES AMERICANAS DE DIABETES Y CARDIOLOGÍA:The American Diabetes and Cardiology Societies are organizations that provide guidelines and consensus on diabetes management and cardiovascular health.", "NUTRIENTES ANTIINFLAMATORIOS:Anti-inflammatory nutrients include fiber, vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants that contribute to reducing inflammation in the body.", "NUTRIENTES PROINFLAMATORIOS:Pro-inflammatory nutrients include refined sugars, starches, trans fats, and high-calorie density foods that can exacerbate inflammation.", "ACEITE DE OLIVA VIRGEN EXTRA:ACEITE DE OLIVA VIRGEN EXTRA, or extra virgin olive oil, is an essential component of the Mediterranean diet. It is widely used for both cooking and dressing dishes, and it is renowned for its numerous health benefits. Notably, this type of olive oil is associated with improved cardiovascular health and is recognized for its role in reducing the risk of type 2 diabetes.", "CIRCUNFERENCIA DE LA CINTURA:Waist circumference is a measure of abdominal fat that can indicate health risks, and it can be reduced through adherence to the Mediterranean diet."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}